# Workspace navigation titles

Every **main module page** (sidebar destination) must use the shared workspace title chrome.

## Required pattern

```swift
.bonsaiWorkspaceNavigationTitle("Module Name")
```

Defined in `BonsaiWorldChrome.swift`. It:

- Places the section title in a real `VStack` **above** workspace content (not `safeAreaInset`)
- Hides the window title via `bonsaiWorldChrome()` → `.toolbar(removing: .title)`
- Aligns leading inset with `DashboardSpacing.pageInset` (or 0 when `faloShellProvidesLeadingInset` is set)

## Why VStack (not safeAreaInset)

`HSplitView` / some split children **ignore** top `safeAreaInset` and draw under the window toolbar, clipping the first lines (seen on Species Library detail). A `VStack` forces content below the title on every page that uses the modifier.

## Do

- Use `bonsaiWorkspaceNavigationTitle` on Trees, Dashboard, Species Library, Knowledge pages, Tasks, Yamadori, Seeds, Soil, Images, Care, Inventory list hubs, Collections, Locations, Work, Settings roots, and new sidebar destinations
- Keep sheet / dialog titles as `.navigationTitle("…")` (modals are not workspace pages)
- When embedding `TreeDetailView` under library chrome, set `showsNavigationTitle: false` so it does not add a second title
- For Settings panes that still clip under the toolbar without this modifier’s layout help, keep `.safeAreaPadding(.top)` (see Botanical Library)

## Do not

- Put the workspace title in `ToolbarItem(placement: .navigation)` — section separator after the label
- Use `safeAreaInset(edge: .top)` for the workspace title around `HSplitView` / Species Library
- Use `ignoresSafeArea(.container, edges: .top)` around `GeometryReader` workspaces (Dashboard crash)
- Wrap title chrome in `GeometryReader` for height
- Add horizontal rules under the page title

## New pages

1. Prefer the two-column shell (`NavigationSplitView` + `splitDetail`) used by Trees / Dashboard
2. Apply `.bonsaiWorkspaceNavigationTitle("…")` once on the workspace root
3. Do not add a title underline or column-title hairline
